content.thinking:
Now I see it. Look at line 248-251:

```css
#wpwrap {
    background: var(--wpds-color-fg-content-neutral, #1e1e1e);
    overflow-y: auto;
}
body {
    background: #fff;
}
```

The `#wpwrap` background is set to `var(--wpds-color-fg-content-neutral, #1e1e1e)` which is a very dark color (#1e1e1e). If the CSS variable isn't defined, it falls back to `#1e1e1e` (dark).


So the React app should be mounting into that container div, but it's not rendering anything. The blank page suggests either a JavaScript error preventing the app from initializing or the WordPress boot module failing to load. The real question is why this works fine with Imagify but breaks with BackWPup—there must be something BackWPup is doing that interferes with the app initialization. I need to check what scripts BackWPup registers in the admin area and whether any of them might be interfering with the script module loading. Let me look at the subscriber files to see what hooks BackWPup is using.

